# T9A

Small web apps for using a HMD feature phone abroad, built for Opera
Mini Extreme on a 2.4" screen. Pages are plain HTML, with no JS or
reliance on CSS.

## Apps (one repo each)
- T9A-mail: read, reply and compose email (Posteo in, Resend out)
- T9A-map: transit directions (Google Routes API)
- T9A-drive: driving directions (Google Routes API)

## How it works
- Each app is a small Bottle app on a VPS. The phone only fetches HTML;
  all API and mail work happens server-side.
- Only one app holds port 80 at a time. A switcher page runs
  `/root/restart <mail|map|drive>`, which stops the others and starts
  the one chosen.
- Secrets live outside git (~/.resendrc, ~/.mbsyncrc, per-app .env).

## Deploy
Edit and commit on a dev machine, then push. On the server:

    git pull
    ./venv/bin/python -m py_compile app.py && echo OK   # map: map.py
    /root/restart <app>

Only restart if OK printed.
